  "observations": [
    "Idle and blurred draft retain a transparent background, one underline, visible same placeholder/draft and vertically centered 18-unit text at matching content width.",
    "Web input box measures 314 by 58 CSS pixels. Native accessibility bounds measure 1099 by 204 physical pixels at density 3.5, approximately 314.286 by 58.286 vp.",
    "System Back leaves both native draft examples unfocused. The native after-IME screenshots therefore pair with blurred Web draft, while real-IME focused screenshots pair for the answer control only.",
    "Web focus uses an offset accent ring and a distinct underline. The native official outline meets the input edge, and the underline and outline join along the lower edge.",
    "Native submit is a full-width rounded rectangle and the Web submit is a compact pill. Input-to-submit gaps measure 16 vp at native rest and 17.14 vp at focus, against 18 and 19 CSS pixels on Web. Hint and completion feedback differ separately.",
    "Both completed states show the matching disabled authoritative answer and no submit. Native rendered text is visibly paler than Web in both themes, before any follow-up fix."
  ],
